$\begin{align*}\sigma&=\sqrt{\frac{15}{16}}\\&=\frac{\sqrt{15}}{4}\end{align*}$

The interval has endpoints $L=\frac{15-\sqrt{15}}{4}$ and $U=\frac{15+\sqrt{15}}{4}$. Both lie within $[0,5]$.

$\begin{align*}P(\mu-\sigma\leq X\leq\mu+\sigma)&=\int_L^U\frac{3x^2}{125}\,dx\\&=\left[\frac{x^3}{125}\right]_L^U\\&=\frac{(15+\sqrt{15})^3-(15-\sqrt{15})^3}{8000}\\&=\frac{1380\sqrt{15}}{8000}\\&=\frac{69\sqrt{15}}{400}\\&\approx0.67\end{align*}$

The shaded area represents this probability.

